.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
is an HTTP server that runs a command when it receives a POST
request signed with a secret.
It is intended to receive webhooks from GitHub.
.Pp
Each exposed directory is a directory under the document root:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
<doc-root>/<directory>/
├── hooks\&.edn           the directory\(aqs secret
├── commands/<command>  each command that can be run
└── log/commands\&.log    the output of each run
.Ed
.Pp
A POST request to
.Ql "/run/<command>/in/<directory>"
(with or without a trailing
.Ql "/" )
runs
.Ql "<doc-root>/<directory>/commands/<command>"
if the request’s
.Ql "X-Hub-Signature-256"
header is the HMAC-SHA256 of its body under the directory’s
secret,
as GitHub sends it.
The response is sent once the command has started;
.Nm
does not wait for the command to finish.
.Pp
.Nm
runs until it is stopped.
It prints the address it is listening on,
then the request line and status of each request to standard
output,
and the reason for each refused request to standard error.
.
