.Sh CONFIGURATION
The configuration file of an exposed directory is one EDN map
with a
.Ql ":secret" ,
a non-empty string:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
{:secret \(dqa long random string\(dq}
.Ed
.Pp
The file is read as data;
nothing in it is evaluated.
It is read on each request,
so a change takes effect without restarting
.Nm .
A file that is missing,
is not a map,
has a key other than
.Ql ":secret"
or has an empty secret refuses every request for its directory.
.Pp
The secret is the one entered in the webhook’s settings on
GitHub.
The webhook’s content type does not matter,
since the signature covers the body as it is sent.
.
.Sh COMMANDS
A command must be an executable file directly in the command
directory.
A symlink in its place is refused,
as is a command directory that resolves to a path outside its
exposed directory.
Directory and command names in the URL can contain letters,
digits,
.Ql "\&." ,
.Ql "_"
and
.Ql "-" ,
and must begin with a letter,
digit or
.Ql "_" .
.Pp
A command is run directly,
not through a shell,
with no arguments.
Its working directory is the command directory and its standard
input is
.Ql "/dev/null" .
Its environment has
.Ql "PATH" ,
.Ql "HOME" ,
.Ql "LANG" ,
.Ql "LC_ALL"
and
.Ql "TZ"
from
.Nm
‘s environment (where set),
.Ql "TENTER_DIRECTORY" ,
the name of the exposed directory,
and
.Ql "TENTER_COMMAND" ,
the name of the command.
Nothing else in
.Nm
’s environment is passed on.
.Pp
Only one run of a command is in progress at a time.
A request that arrives during a run is answered with
.Ql "Command queued" ,
and the command runs once more when the run ends,
however many requests arrived.
Different commands run at the same time.
.
.Sh LOG
The standard output and standard error of each run are appended
to the log as the command writes them.
A run begins with an
.Ql "Initiating:"
line and ends with a
.Ql "Finished:"
line that gives the exit status,
or a
.Ql "Failed:"
line if the command could not be started (for example,
a script without a
.Ql "#!"
line).
Each line begins with the local time:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
\(lB2026-11-20 11:47:38 +0900\(rB Initiating: /var/www/example/commands/rebuild
\(lB2026-11-20 11:47:38 +0900\(rB Building\&.\&.\&.
\(lB2026-11-20 11:47:41 +0900\(rB Finished: /var/www/example/commands/rebuild \*(lpexit status 0\*(rp
.Ed
.Pp
If the log cannot be opened,
the command is not run.
.
.Sh RESPONSES
Each response is plain text and closes the connection.
.Pp
.Bl -bullet -offset 3n -compact
.It
.Ic 200
.Ql "Command initiated"
or
.Ql "Command queued" .
.It
.Ic 400
.Ql "X-Hub-Signature-256 header not set" ,
.Ql "Command not found"
or
.Ql "Bad request" .
.It
.Ic 403
.Ql "X-Hub-Signature-256 header did not match" .
This is the response to a wrong signature,
to an unknown directory and to a directory with a configuration
file that cannot be used,
so that the response does not show which.
.It
.Ic 404
for any other path and
.Ic 405
for any method but POST.
.It
.Ic 408
if the request is not sent within 10 seconds.
.It
.Ic 411
without
.Ql "Content-Length" ,
.Ic 413
for a body over 1 MiB,
.Ic 431
for headers over 16 KiB and
.Ic 501
with
.Ql "Transfer-Encoding" .
.It
.Ic 500
if the log cannot be opened.
.It
.Ic 503
when 32 connections are already being handled.
.El
.
.Sh SECURITY
.Nm
runs programs for anyone who has a directory’s secret.
Use a long random secret,
and keep the configuration file readable only by the user that
runs
.Nm .
.Pp
.Nm
does not use TLS.
Run it on a loopback address behind a reverse proxy,
such as nginx,
that provides HTTPS.
Without TLS,
the secret is not sent,
but the payload can be read in transit and a captured request
can be sent again.
A signature covers only the body,
so a request can be sent again in any case;
it runs the command again.
.Pp
Run
.Nm
as an unprivileged user,
not as root.
Commands run as the same user.
.Pp
Once it is listening,
.Nm
gives up the capabilities it does not need,
including compiling code,
reading the environment and making outbound connections.
.
.Sh EXAMPLES
Serve the directories in
.Ql "/srv/www"
on port 9000:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
$ tenter -r /srv/www -p 9000
Listening on http://127\&.0\&.0\&.1:9000/
.Ed
.Pp
Send a signed request with
.Ql "curl"
and
.Ql "openssl" :
.Bd -literal -offset indent
$ body=\(aq{}\(aq
$ sig=$\*(lpprintf \(aq%s\(aq \(dq$body\(dq | openssl dgst -sha256 -hmac \(dq$SECRET\(dq | sed \(aqs/\&.* //\(aq\*(rp
$ curl -X POST -H \(dqX-Hub-Signature-256: sha256=$sig\(dq --data \(dq$body\(dq \e
    http://127\&.0\&.0\&.1:9000/run/rebuild/in/example/
Command initiated
.Ed
.
.Sh EXIT STATUS
.Nm
exits with 1 if its options are invalid or it cannot listen.
It otherwise runs until it is stopped.
.
